      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet C1 is drawn with the value 0.1 µF / 16 V.",
      "expected": "Per the spec this position belongs to the PDI 'C2 default' group, which should be 1 µF / 25 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver sheet: 'C1' with value '0.1uF/16V' beside L1/Display_Power_Switch"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "A 10x-low capacitance and a lower voltage rating (16 V vs 25 V) on the EPD supply decoupling reduces boost stability/margin and derates the part below the intended rail.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The EPD driver sheet's capacitor values deviate from the intended design: C2 is a 1 nF/6.3 V part where the spec calls for 1 µF/6.3 V, and C1 is 0.1 µF/16 V where the spec calls for 1 µF/25 V. Both are in the EPD boost/charge-pump supply, so the e-paper display would not be driven as intended."
}

